    <string name="config_permission_usb_row">🔌 ADB over USB (from the PC gateway)</string>
    <string name="config_permission_usb_dialog_title">ADB over USB</string>
    <string name="config_permission_usb_dialog_message">A phone can\'t pair with itself over a USB cable — this path activates from the desktop gateway (PC), not from here.\n\n1. Turn on Developer options (button below) and inside it, "USB debugging".\n2. Connect the phone to the PC with a USB cable.\n3. Open Kairos\' gateway on the PC and use "Activate over USB" — it\'ll ask you to tap "Allow" on this phone the first time.\n4. Done: the gateway turns off the background process limiter and exempts Kairos from battery optimization, same as the wireless path.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_credits_row">ℹ Credits — root / ADB / Shizuku</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_step1_title">Step 1 of 2 — Wireless debugging</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_step1_message">Open Developer options, go into \"Wireless debugging\" and tap \"Pair device with pairing code\" — you\'ll see a port and a 6-digit code. Also note the connection port shown next to the IP, on the main Wireless debugging screen.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_step2_title">Step 2 of 2 — Pairing details</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_step2_message">Fill in the 3 values Settings showed you. The code expires quickly — if it fails, repeat step 1 for a new one.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_progress_title">Pairing ADB</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_progress_pairing">Installing android-tools and pairing…</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_success">Wireless ADB paired and connected — you can use it as a privilege provider now.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_error_install">Could not install android-tools</string>
    <string name="config_permission_adb_error_connect">Could not connect — check the code hasn\'t expired and the 3 values are correct</string>
    <string name="config_permission_shizuku_dialog_title">Shizuku is not available</string>
    <string name="config_permission_shizuku_dialog_message">Install the Shizuku app, start its service (via wireless ADB or root, from the Shizuku app itself) and follow its instructions to export \"rish\" to your $HOME — once done, this row will show \"Available\".</string>
