    <string name="config_permission_credits_title">Credits — permission mechanisms</string>
    <string name="config_permission_credits_message">Shizuku (github.com/RikkaApps/Shizuku) — Apache License 2.0.\n\nShizuku-API (github.com/RikkaApps/Shizuku-API) — MIT License, © RikkaW.\n\nAndroid-Automation-Termux-Shizuku-Rish — Apache License 2.0.\n\ntermux-shizuku-tools (github.com/AlexeiCrystal/termux-shizuku-tools) — license not confirmed for this project (its README links to a LICENCE.md not present in the local copy used for this research).\n\nAndroid Debug Bridge (adb), used by the desktop gateway for the USB path — Google/AOSP, Apache License 2.0 (dl.google.com/android/repository, platform-tools).\n\nNone of these projects were copied — they were only used as reference for which permission mechanisms to offer (root, wireless ADB, USB ADB, Shizuku); Kairos never uses exploits or CVEs to escalate privileges.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_shizuku_manage_other_apps_row">Grant Shizuku to other apps</string>
    <string name="config_permission_shizuku_manage_other_apps_title">Shizuku permissions for other apps</string>
    <string name="config_permission_shizuku_manage_other_apps_message">The row above only requests Shizuku permission for Kairos/Termux. Granting (or reviewing) another installed app\'s Shizuku permission can\'t be done from Kairos — that\'s reserved to the Shizuku (or Shizuku+) app itself, which is the only one that manages those permissions. We\'ll open Shizuku so you can do it there.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_shizuku_manage_other_apps_open">Open Shizuku</string>
    <string name="config_permission_dhizuku_check_row">Check Dhizuku (no external app)</string>
    <string name="config_permission_dhizuku_check_title">Dhizuku — elevated permissions without any external app</string>
    <string name="config_permission_dhizuku_eligible_message">This device has no accounts configured — Android would allow activating Dhizuku (Device Owner) via ADB, without installing Shizuku or any other app. This screen only checks eligibility: actually activating it is a high-risk action (reverting it badly can require a factory reset) that is not implemented yet — it will be researched further once it can be tested on a real dedicated device.</string>
    <string name="config_permission_dhizuku_not_eligible_message">This device has at least one account configured (Google or other) — Android does not allow activating Dhizuku (Device Owner) this way, that\'s a real system restriction. Using it would require a device with no accounts at all (factory-fresh, or after removing them all).</string>
